{"task_id": "HumanEval/14", "solution": "import unittest\ndef all_prefixes(string: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a list of all prefixes of a given string, from shortest to longest.\n\n    Args:\n        string: The input string.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of strings, where each string is a prefix of the input string,\n        ordered from shortest to longest. An empty list is returned if the\n        input string is empty.\n\n    Examples:\n        >>> all_prefixes(\"abc\")\n        ['a', 'ab', 'abc']\n        >>> all_prefixes(\"hello\")\n        ['h', 'he', 'hel', 'hell', 'hello']\n        >>> all_prefixes(\"\")\n        []\n        >>> all_prefixes(\"\u4f60\u597d\")\n        ['\u4f60', '\u4f60\u597d']\n    \"\"\"\n    if not string:\n        return []\n    return [string[:i] for i in range(1, len(string) + 1)]"}
