{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "def encrypt(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return a Caesar cipher of *s* by shifting each alphabetic character forward by\n    four places in the alphabet. Non\u2011alphabetic characters are left unchanged.\n    \n    Parameters\n    ----------\n    s : str\n        The input string to encrypt.\n    \n    Returns\n    -------\n    str\n        The encrypted string.\n    \n    Examples\n    --------\n    >>> encrypt('hi')\n    'lm'\n    >>> encrypt('asdfghjkl')\n    'ewhjklnop'\n    >>> encrypt('gf')\n    'kj'\n    >>> encrypt('et')\n    'ix'\n    \"\"\"\n    def shift_char(c: str) -> str:\n        if 'a' <= c <= 'z':\n            return chr((ord(c) - ord('a') + 4) % 26 + ord('a'))\n        if 'A' <= c <= 'Z':\n            return chr((ord(c) - ord('A') + 4) % 26 + ord('A'))\n        return c\n\n    return ''.join(shift_char(ch) for ch in s)"}
