{"task_id": "HumanEval/124", "solution": "def valid_date(date: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validate a date string in the format mm-dd-yyyy.\n\n    Rules:\n    1. The string must not be empty.\n    2. The month must be between 1 and 12.\n    3. The day must be within the appropriate range for the month:\n       * 31-day months: 1,3,5,7,8,10,12\n       * 30-day months: 4,6,9,11\n       * February: 1-29 (not accounting for leap years)\n    4. The format must be mm-dd-yyyy with exactly two digits for month and day\n       and four digits for year, separated by hyphens.\n\n    Args:\n        date: The date string to validate.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the date is valid, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not date:\n        return False\n\n    # Check format: mm-dd-yyyy with hyphens\n    parts = date.split(\"-\")\n    if len(parts) != 3:\n        return False\n    month_str, day_str, year_str = parts\n    if (\n        len(month_str) != 2\n        or len(day_str) != 2\n        or len(year_str) != 4\n        or not (month_str.isdigit() and day_str.isdigit() and year_str.isdigit())\n    ):\n        return False\n\n    month = int(month_str)\n    day = int(day_str)\n    # year is not checked for validity beyond being digits\n\n    # Month bounds\n    if month < 1 or month > 12:\n        return False\n\n    # Day bounds per month\n    if month in {1, 3, 5, 7, 8, 10, 12}:\n        return 1 <= day <= 31\n    if month in {4, 6, 9, 11}:\n        return 1 <= day <= 30\n    # month == 2\n    return 1 <= day <= 29"}
